MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS: [
  "single-linkage chaining is a textbook clustering pathology (Jain & Dubes 1988; Hastie/Tibshirani/Friedman §14.3.12) — connected-components on a graph with edges = pairwise-above-T is single-linkage, and Jaccard-above-T is provably non-transitive (triangle inequality fails for 1-J at T>=0.5), so chain-endpoint-distance growing without bound is mathematically forced, not emergent",
  "complete-linkage giving innocent-removal=0 is the *definition* of complete-linkage (every pair in the kept cluster is above T), not a discovered mitigation — this is the textbook fix for chaining and has been known since the 1960s",
  "the 0.724 headline is a function of the synthetic corpus mix (8x10 chains over ~N docs at moderate density): the harness CONSTRUCTS drift-chains with consec Jaccard ~0.82 > T=0.8, then measures the fraction of chain-members deleted — by construction, almost all non-endpoint chain-docs will have max-sim-to-rep < T",
  "EXACT > MinHash effect size (0.724 vs 0.323) is exactly what k=128 MinHash variance predicts (per-edge SE on J~0.82 is ~sqrt(0.82*0.18/128)≈0.034; marginal chain edges near T drop out probabilistically), so this is consistent with basic estimator theory, not evidence against an LSH-FP explanation in any non-trivial sense"
]
CONFOUNDS: [
  "corpus-construction confound: 'innocent-removal fraction' is dominated by how many CHAIN docs the generator injected vs CLIQUE+SINGLETON docs — the density sweep (0.36→0.94) tracks the chain-to-non-chain ratio almost mechanically",
  "rep-selection confound: 'lowest-id' representative is a worst-case for chain-endpoint similarity; centroid/medoid or density-weighted rep would change innocent-removal under CC without changing the graph — the claim is conflating CC-merge-policy with rep-selection-policy",
  "threshold-vs-drift confound: the headline depends on the specific gap (consec=0.82 vs T=0.8) the generator chose; at T=0.9 effect collapses to 0 (researcher-flagged), so the result is really 'effect exists in a narrow (T, drift)-band the harness sits in'",
  "the 'realistic operating point' label for T=0.8 is doing load-bearing work but is unjustified within L0 — Lee2021 NearDup uses different (n-gram, threshold) regimes; calling 0.8 'realistic' is a claim about real corpora, not a property of the harness"
]
ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED: [
