  "that single-linkage chaining producing far endpoint-pairs is novel beyond 60-year-old clustering literature applied to dedup graphs — the contribution-vs-folklore question is unaddressed",
  "that 'innocent' (Jaccard<T to retained rep) is the right *loss* function — a doc could be deleted while being semantically redundant with the kept doc via a different metric, in which case the deletion is not actually harmful (the L1 (c) currency question)",
